                <pb facs="0860" n="851" sameAs="frus:frus1938v05/pg851"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.2331/112</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Peru</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 654</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Lima</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1938-09-17"
                            >September 17, 1938</date>.<lb/>[Received September 27.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Department’s strictly
                    confidential instruction No. 164, of September 7, 1938, I have the honor to
                    report that the note attached thereto was delivered to the Foreign Office on
                    September 16th. There is enclosed a memorandum of the conversation which took
                    place on that occasion.</p>
                <p>Respectfully yours,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Louis G. Dreyfus,
                    Jr</hi>.</signed></closer>



